# Feature: User work dashboard & task timer

**The UI timer is informational only.** All state transitions and timestamps
are decided and stamped by the server.

## State machine
| Current state | Allowed action | Next state | Server validation |
|---|---|---|---|
| PENDING | START | RUNNING | Employee has no other RUNNING task; task is assigned and open |
| RUNNING | HOLD | ON_HOLD | `HoldReasonId` is mandatory |
| ON_HOLD | RESUME | RUNNING | Task is not completed/cancelled |
| RUNNING / ON_HOLD | END | COMPLETED / CHECKING | Completion status, output remark, and required files/checklist validated |
| IDLE / ON_HOLD | OFFICE_CLOSE | Office session closed | No RUNNING task allowed |

## Timer calculation
```
ActualWorkSeconds = SUM(seconds between each START/RESUME and the next HOLD/END)
HoldSeconds        = SUM(seconds between each HOLD and the next RESUME/END)
TotalElapsedSeconds = EndTime - FirstStartTime
ActualWorkSeconds + HoldSeconds <= TotalElapsedSeconds   // always true
```
- Store all timestamps in UTC; convert to local time only for display.
- Never compute active time from `Task.StartedAt`/`CompletedAt` alone - always
  pair `TaskTimeEvent` rows.
- `TaskTimeEvent` is append-only. If connectivity drops mid-RUNNING, the task
  stays RUNNING server-side until a later valid event or an authorized
  adjustment record - never silently auto-closed by a client reconnect.
- Only one active RUNNING task per employee unless a future rule explicitly
  enables multi-task time splitting.

## Hold reasons (none count as active work time)
| Code | Reason | KPI treatment |
|---|---|---|
| OTHER_WORK | Other work | Reported separately as possible reassignment load |
| LUNCH | Lunch break | Excluded from task time and delay blame |
| TEA | Tea break | Excluded |
| WAIT_APPROVAL | Waiting for approval | Delay attributed to approval dependency |
| WAIT_MATERIAL | Waiting for material | Delay attributed to material dependency |
| MACHINE_NA | Machine not available | Delay attributed to machine capacity |
| MEETING | Meeting | Excluded from active task time |
| PERSONAL | Personal break | Excluded |
| OFFICE_CLOSE | Office time close | Must not be used while a task is RUNNING |

## Pseudo transaction for START (apply the same rigor to HOLD/RESUME/END)
```
BEGIN TRANSACTION
  SELECT active task for EmployeeId WITH lock
  IF another RUNNING task exists -> reject 409
  Validate requested TaskId belongs to employee and is startable
  INSERT TaskTimeEvent(START, ServerUtcNow)
  UPDATE DesignTask SET Status='RUNNING', StartedAt=COALESCE(StartedAt, ServerUtcNow)
COMMIT
```

## API
- `POST /api/tasks/{id}/start`, `/hold`, `/resume`, `/end`
- `POST /api/workday/close` - rejects if a running task exists
- `GET /api/tasks/my` - current user's task list
